{% if impact_nodes %}
## Blast radius

What this change touches, and the unchanged code that depends on it. These
consumer files are NOT under review: they are evidence about the changed lines.
Do not report a finding on a consumer line. When a change breaks one of them,
anchor the finding to the changed line responsible, name the consumer file in
`evidence_files`, and use `evidence: contract`.

A boundary listed as `contained` was searched and nothing outside the change used
it. One listed as `no references found` was searched by name only: an alias, a
re-export or a runtime lookup would not have matched, so it is not proof of
anything.
{% for node in impact_nodes %}
### `{{ node.name }}` — {{ node.kind }} in `{{ node.file }}`:{{ node.line }} — {{ node.status }}
{% if node.note %}
{{ node.note }}
{% endif %}
{% for consumer in node.consumers %}
- `{{ consumer.path }}`:{{ consumer.line }} ({{ consumer.relation }})
{% if consumer.snippet %}
```
{{ consumer.snippet }}
```
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
